  "recap": "The Base Invaders put together their best offensive showing of the season on Tuesday, July 28, outslugging the Bad Knees Bears 22-13. The bats were relentless from top to bottom, with 34 team hits and 10 different players reaching base, turning the game into a track meet early and never letting the Bears back in. Jason had the night of his life, going 6-for-6 with 7 RBI and a home run, while Brendan matched him for power with a 5-for-6, 3 RBI, 1 HR performance of his own. Scotty added 4 RBI on a 4-for-5 night, Sean chipped in 4-for-4 with 3 RBI, and Katie drove in 2 runs to round out a lineup that had an answer for everything the Bears threw at them. It was the kind of night that made a 9-run margin feel almost tight given how much offense was on display, and the Base Invaders will take the momentum into their next game.",
